<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I89d9f2217c87fc76526375464c07d12227198d46" commit="dcd110c840110d9c571ece14a6bb010303c2f3d0" commit_message="autotest(wifi): Correct wait_for_service_states parameters(1/2).  The |wait_for_service_states| RPC call expects an array of strings in |states| parameter. Correcting a bug in the syntax for single length tuples which causes a type mismatch error on Brillo native proxy RPC server (i.e ('idle') instead of ('idle',)). Changing this parameter to array instead of tuple in all invocations. This is already the case for some other tests like network_WiFi_ProfileBasic, etc.  BUG=25323465 TEST=`test_that $host --board=$BOARD network_WiFi_ChannelHop` and `test_that $host --board=$BOARD network_WiFi_RetryConnectHidden` on dragonboard.  Change-Id: I89d9f2217c87fc76526375464c07d12227198d46 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308531 Commit-Ready: Roshan Pius &lt;rpius@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Roshan Pius &lt;rpius@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: mukesh agrawal &lt;quiche@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308531" owner_email="rpius@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/31/308531/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I98ce5429bc8c25f14ca685699e7ef570943f6270" commit="7864410e9bde54c0155aaec992b3a64ecb6271fc" commit_message="autotest(wifi): Correct wait_for_service_states parameters(2/2)  Convert the |timeout_seconds| parameter to int in |wait_for_connection| since the native XML Rpc server expects an int. int/float values can be interchangeably used in Python server, but not when interoping with a native server.  BUG=25323465 TEST=`test_that $host --board=$BOARD network_WiFi_RetryConnectHidden` on dragonboard.  Change-Id: I98ce5429bc8c25f14ca685699e7ef570943f6270 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309263 Commit-Ready: Roshan Pius &lt;rpius@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Roshan Pius &lt;rpius@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: mukesh agrawal &lt;quiche@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309263" owner_email="rpius@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/63/309263/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie6b1d74eaac4d6c38d52641626966b5d3ce63bd3" commit="53edd3700bdb11a55f5e7afabc59076dae8c1193" commit_message="driver: si114x: Fail init of proximity sensor if light sensor fails.  If init of the light sensor fails (for instance, the chip is not present on the i2c bus), we need to fail the init of the proximity sensor. Otherwise, the EC will report an unexistent sensor to the AP.  BRANCH=smaug BUG=chrome-os-partner:46638 TEST=check the proximity sensor is not reported if sensor is disconnected from the main board.  Change-Id: Ie6b1d74eaac4d6c38d52641626966b5d3ce63bd3 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308560 Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308560" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/60/308560/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I647f83580240bf5ba0c340fca3184220abe4c12e" commit="cbf1f37f78ac672b89c4c1c64a59b3c2709e2f05" commit_message="motion: Remove duplicate shutdown code  Call shutdown() entry point at init() and remove duplicate code. shutdown would init the sensor so they would be ready if needed. Set S5 flag to include G3 (hard off) state, not only S5 (soft off).  BUG=chrome-os-partner:45722 BRANCH=smaug TEST=When doing a RO-&gt;RW transition while AP is in G3, check the sensors are initialized properly. This issue was found while testng the magic sequence code.  Change-Id: I647f83580240bf5ba0c340fca3184220abe4c12e Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308561 Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308561" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/61/308561/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I875f18f85aa6d942431996161aeb8f9ebaf2913b" commit="552f2628a1f5f07b721f353b8f465f061275ba41" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: renormalize splitconfigs  Renormalize splitconfig after remove unused flavour config for rockchip and ipq806x.  Run chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig oldconfig and accept the defaults. BUG=none TEST=none Signed-off-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I875f18f85aa6d942431996161aeb8f9ebaf2913b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307451 Commit-Ready: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kan Yan &lt;kyan@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307451" owner_email="kyan@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/307451/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibfdfed4a9a19278b123029fea08b2b4e6dd99807" commit="89acb704f08572bf63096adc6c79b6f27af87f88" commit_message="CRAS: iodev - Allow 2+ channels with default channel layout  This patch generates a default channel layout based on the matched best channel count, instead of hardcoding to stereo. The default layout follows the channel order defined in enum CRAS_CHANNEL.  This patch allows 4 channel recording even when no PCM channel map is provided by the kernel, which is the case for ASoC cards. Channel layout info isn't very useful for mic arrays. The mic array geometry should be provided by UCM config flag &quot;MicPositions&quot;.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43037 TEST=4 channel recording on Buddy cras_test_client --rate 48000 --num_channels 4 --capture_file /tmp/4ch_cras.wav  Change-Id: Ibfdfed4a9a19278b123029fea08b2b4e6dd99807 Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309286 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309286" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/86/309286/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ibc223a41497392f39baf1751c8631d52cf455633" commit="4dc7d514a2ec9bca3845a87bf450485103aa984b" commit_message="nouveau/drm: Enables ELPG.(Engine Level Power Gating).  Enables ELPG after GR init &amp; Golden context save is over. ELPG will power gate GR engine, when GR engine remains IDLE for some Threshold time.  BUG=none TEST=See elpg_stats in debugfs  Change-Id: Ibc223a41497392f39baf1751c8631d52cf455633 Signed-off-by: Deepak Goyal &lt;dgoyal@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309102 Commit-Ready: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@nvidia.com&gt; Tested-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309102" owner_email="markz@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/02/309102/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib3ae4f0cd2b7eac0dbf468460c053c10b7c37752" commit="c23ee745c84573a36217e5fad876fe5f5f3c8a2f" commit_message="Add dhcp_client from AOSP  BUG=b:25323659 TEST=copy it to .repo/manifests/full.xml, repo sync and note source code under src/aosp/system/connectivity/  Change-Id: Ib3ae4f0cd2b7eac0dbf468460c053c10b7c37752 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309312 Commit-Ready: Ningyuan Wang &lt;nywang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ningyuan Wang &lt;nywang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Zeping Qiu &lt;zqiu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309312" owner_email="nywang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/12/309312/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I507d408ff3be6edcd15c24b6769ca6d4468a0d14" commit="3e295c61b3bb527f54b2f496846bc7c11664cc0b" commit_message="Modernize EditBookmarksEnabled and RestoreOnStartupURLs.  This CL enhances two older tests, policy_EditBookmarksEnabled and policy_RestoreOnStartupURLs, to incorporate recent improvements inspired by and implemented in later tests. In summary: 1) Test Cases are stored in a dictionary, not a list. 2) Test Case dictionary includes the default policy values. 3) Test Cases are ordered (by name) for execution and listing. 4) Use the 'is_value_given' flag to control whether the test case uses the default values or the user-specified values.  BUG=None TEST=Run test_that &lt;IP&gt; policy_EditBookmarksEnabled and policy_RestoreOnStartupURLs.  Change-Id: I507d408ff3be6edcd15c24b6769ca6d4468a0d14 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308518 Commit-Ready: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Cunningham &lt;scunningham@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Haddock &lt;dhaddock@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308518" owner_email="scunningham@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/18/308518/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I0bf76280518bf4e3aa2162717d4b17c4bdb335f2" commit="7d15657cbaef72091694b2680b53640ab6cc199e" commit_message="drm/nouveau/pmu/gk20a: Update dvfs algorithm  - Instead of looking at average load, we ramp up based on immediate   utilization. - We inhibit ramping down for a few ticks after we ramp up, letting   the average become realistic.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46754 TEST=scroll the home screen, see no jank  Change-Id: I0bf76280518bf4e3aa2162717d4b17c4bdb335f2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309260 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309260" owner_email="marcheu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/60/309260/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I9089755b75118499bec37bdb96d1635f66252e65" commit="518f87b1ddea571281859deb618e355f79486487" commit_message="rk3288: If we fail to read the EDID 5 times in a row, it's an error  Previously if we tried to read the HDMI EDID several times and failed each time then we're return from hdmi_read_edid() with no error.  Then we'd interpret whatever happened to be in memory at the time as an EDID--not so great.  Let's actually look at the error.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:46256 TEST=Monitor that can't read EDID not shows that in the log  Change-Id: I908